	SGDK's XGM sound driver for the z80, and the short XGM sequence that silences it.
	Copyright Stephane Dallongeville, MIT licensed, which permits copying with attribution.

	xgm.bin is 5888 bytes of assembled z80 code, taken byte for byte out of drv_xgm.o's
	.rodata section in vendor/SGDK/lib/libmd.a, which is where SGDK's own link takes it from.
	Its source is vendor/SGDK/src/snd/drv_xgm.s80, and assembling that needs sjasm, so the
	assembled form is carried here rather than the source: a build of this SDK then needs
	neither SGDK nor sjasm.

		md5  9923df157defdef8c67f259788556e4b

	xgm-stop.bin is 172 bytes, copied from vendor/SGDK/res/sound/stop_xgm.bin. It is an XGM
	music stream that turns every channel off and then ends, which is what md.Sound.stop
	hands the driver in place of the tune it was playing.

	silence.bin beside them is 256 zero bytes written here, not copied: it is the null PCM
	sample every unused sample slot points at, and a sample of silence is zeroes on any
	machine.
